# The tutorial tour's helpers that point a note at a rectangle of one of the game's screens (see tutwin.c): the centre of a made-up
# rectangle as a point on each of the four screens (the answer, x * 10000 + y, is in the open_result region; the screens are not
# open, so their positions are what the game keeps for them), the plain centre, and the notes that point at it (Return closes each).
25 load
26 state tw_fields 0x8cc1e4 0x5c
26 state tw_flags 0x8cc244 8
44 open tut_rect_base
48 snap rect-base
50 open tut_rect_iface
54 snap rect-iface
56 open tut_rect_soc
60 snap rect-soc
62 open tut_rect_des
66 snap rect-des
68 open tut_centre
72 snap centre
74 open tut_do_base
80 snap do-base
82 key Return
86 open tut_do_iface
92 snap do-iface
94 key Return
98 open tut_do_soc
104 snap do-soc
106 key Return
110 open tut_do_des
116 snap do-des
118 key Return
122 snap closed
124 close
# The base screen can open under the notes (Return reaches the game too): its leader portraits (and a pixel at the left panel's corner) animate slower than a snap's burst.
mask 265 625 310 680
mask 700 625 760 680
mask 134 709 138 713
